---
title: Lemon & Blueberry Oat Bites
author: graze
servings: 12
description: No-bake wholegrain oat flapjack bites with lemon curd, dried blueberries and seeds - a homemade take on the classic lemon & blueberry flapjack.
---

Line a #20cm square tin{} with baking paper.

Melt @golden syrup{100%g} and @butter{75%g} together in a #saucepan over low heat, stirring, until smooth and runny.

Take off the heat and stir in @light brown sugar{25%g} until dissolved.

Stir in @lemon curd{40%g}, the zest of @lemon, zested{1} and a few drops of @lemon extract{} until fully combined and smooth.

Add @rolled oats{220%g}, @dried blueberries, chopped{40%g}, @sunflower seeds{15%g} and @pumpkin seeds{10%g} to the pan and mix well until everything is fully coated.

Stir in a pinch of @salt{1%pinch}.

Tip the mixture into the lined tin and press down firmly and evenly with the back of a spoon or spatula.

Chill in the fridge for at least ~chill{1%hour}, or until firm.

Turn out and cut into 12 bars or bites.

> Store in an airtight container in the fridge for up to a week.

> Swap dried blueberries for dried cranberries if you can't find them.

> A pinch of baobab or acai powder mixed in with the oats gives a closer flavour match to the original, if you have some.
